        "worked_solution": "To express the number in Cartesian form, we expand the parentheses and substitute the values of the cosine and sine.\n\nSince $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\frac{\\pi }{6}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ and $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\frac{\\pi }{6}=\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =2(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{6})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =2(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+\\text{i}\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}+\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
